  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Awadhesh @ Kallu Sharma vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 May, 2024 Author: Sunita Yadav Bench: Sunita Yadav 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Smt. Justice Sunita Yadav ON THE 20 th OF MAY, 2024 MISC. CRIMINAL CASE No. 13603 of 2024 BETWEEN:- AWADHESH @ KALLU SHARMA S/O RAMDAS SHARMA, AGED ABOUT 40 YEARS, R/O STATION ROAD, GOHAD CHAURAHA DISTRICT BHIND (MADHYA PRADESH) (BY SHRI SANJAY KUMAR BAHIRANI - ADVOCATE) AND THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH STATION POLICE STATION GOHAD CHAURAHA, DISTRICT BHIND (MADHYA PRADESH) (BY SHRI ROHIT MISHRA - ADDITIONAL ADVOCATE GENERAL) This application coming on for admission this day, the following: ORDER Awadhesh @ Kallu Sharma vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/178692495/ 1",
    "facts": "In presence of independent witnesses, seven samples of adulterated substance were taken, shop was sealed and seizure memo was prepared under the Food Safety Act, 2006 and sent to the concerned Laboratory for testing. On the basis of aforesaid, a case was registered against the applicant.",
    "arguments": "Further argument is that if the sample found to be unsafe then prior making the prosecution, the sanction is required from the Commissioner u/S. 42(3) of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 but in the present case no sanction has been obtained from the Commissioner. It is further argued that in case sample is found to be sub-standard and adulterated then prosecution cannot initiate any criminal action because u/Ss. 51 & 57 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 only penalty can be imposed and no imprisonment is provided under such offences. In support of his submissions, counsel for the applicant relied upon the decisions of Apex Court in the case of Ram Nath Vs. The State of U.P. passed in Cr.A. No.472 of 2012 decided on 21/02/2024 and in the case of Sushil Kumar Gupta Vs. State of West Bengal arising out of SLP (Crl.) No.15495 of 2023 decided on 22.03.2024. Under these circumstances, he prays for grant of anticipatory bail to the applicant. O n the other hand, learned State counsel vehemently opposed the application and prayed for its rejection."
  },
